---
/**
 * Ecosystem — positions ASD in the AgentStateLabs stack.
 * ASG (substrate) → CTXone (project memory) + ASD (code-level) as peers.
 */
---

<section class="section ecosystem">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="eyebrow">
			<span class="eyebrow-text">ECOSYSTEM //</span>
		</div>
		<h2 class="section-title">A layer in the AgentStateLabs stack.</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			ASD is a peer to CTXone on top of the AgentStateGraph substrate.
			Three products, one consistent mental model. Pick what you need —
			they compose but don't require each other.
		</p>

		<div class="stack">
			<div class="card substrate">
				<div class="card-tag">SUBSTRATE</div>
				<h4>AgentStateGraph</h4>
				<div class="url">agentstategraph.dev</div>
				<p>
					Content-addressed, versioned, branchable state store.
					Merkle DAG, intent chains, authority + confidence metadata.
					ASD persists everything there — symbols, ledger entries,
					effects, traces.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="peers">
				<div class="card peer">
					<div class="card-tag">PROJECT MEMORY</div>
					<h4>CTXone</h4>
					<div class="url">ctxone.com</div>
					<p>
						Session memory, recall, project-level context for agents.
						Code-agnostic. ASD's <code>matched_policy</code> and
						<code>why_did_we</code> queries cross-reference naturally
						with CTXone facts.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card peer self">
					<div class="card-tag tag-self">YOU ARE HERE</div>
					<h4>AgentStateDeveloper</h4>
					<div class="url">agentstatedeveloper.dev</div>
					<p>
						Code-level context and audit overlay. Semantic index,
						decision ledger, declared + observed effects, call graph,
						policy gate, ratification workflow, audit event stream —
						keyed to symbols in your source tree.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.ecosystem {
		padding: 5rem 0;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.stack {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.peers {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.card {
		background: var(--asd-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-lg);
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.substrate {
		border-left: 3px solid var(--asd-border-hi);
	}

	.peer {
		border-left: 3px solid var(--asd-border-hi);
	}

	.self {
		border-left: 3px solid var(--asd-accent);
		background: rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.04);
	}

	.card-tag {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.62rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--asd-text-faint);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.tag-self {
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
	}

	h4 {
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
	}

	.url {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--asd-text-faint);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	p {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--asd-text-dim);
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin: 0;
	}

	p code {
		background: var(--asd-panel-hi);
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-sm);
		font-size: 0.82em;
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.peers {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
